course: dictionary
lesson: 9208
title: One word, four meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word sole has four meanings, so context tells you which one to use. Look at the words around it first. «Red pandas have fur on the soles of their feet» is about the body, so sole means the bottom of your foot.
explain: Shoes use the same word. «The bumpy soles of your shoes are made to grip» means the bottom part of a shoe or boot. Sole can also be a flat sea fish that people eat, as in «grilled sole on the menu».
explain: When sole is an adjective, it means only, the one and only. «She was the sole survivor of the crash» means she was the only one who lived. To check, swap in a meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Sole is a noun and an adjective.
fact: As a noun, sole means the bottom of your foot, the bottom part of a shoe or boot, or a flat sea fish that people eat.
fact: As an adjective, sole means only: «the sole survivor» is the only one left.
fact: «Soles» means more than one sole, as in «rubber soles» on trainers.
fact: Phrases to know: «the sole of your foot», «sole owner», «sole purpose».
exercise: «Red pandas have fur on the soles of their feet.» Where is the fur? | On their tails | On their ears | *On the bottom of their feet | On their backs
exercise: What are the soles of a shoe? | The laces | *The bottom part of a shoe or boot | The tongue at the front | The top of the heel
exercise: «Maya was the sole person who knew the answer.» What does sole mean here? | Tallest | Quietest | *Only | Oldest
test: «The fish owl grabs salmon with rough, spiky soles.» In this sentence, soles are the bottoms of the owl's feet. | It means rubber shoes | False | *True | It means a flat sea fish
test: Lily ordered grilled sole at the seaside cafe. What is sole here? | A small brown bird | A type of rubber | The bottom of a boat | *A flat sea fish that people eat
exam: «His sole purpose was to find the lost dog.» Which word means the same as sole here? | Most expensive | *Only | Loudest | Happiest
